# ApexYard

> ApexYard gives your coding agents a team's process. The Gate checks every pull request on GitHub. The framework is open source (MIT).

## Your agents write the code. Your team decides what merges.

ApexYard gives your agents a team's process. On GitHub, it holds each pull request until the checks pass and a named person approves.

The Gate checks pull requests from any agent. Build runs in Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and OpenCode.

- 420 pull requests in ApexYard's own repository went through the gate in the last 90 days.
- 3 checks on every pull request from the first day: a linked ticket, a decision record and a review. Named approval when your team is ready.

## What the GitHub App can see

The App cannot open the files in your repository: it has no Contents permission. From each pull request it takes only the names of the changed files, never the code.

- Pull requests: read. Titles, descriptions, reviews and the list of changed files.
- Checks: write. To post the ApexYard check on each pull request.
- Metadata: read. Repository names, and who can write to each repository.
- Members: read. To confirm who can manage your organisation when you sign in.

The check blocks a merge only when you make it required in GitHub. You can remove the App at any time.

## One process, three places

Build puts your agents through tickets, plans and reviews. The Gate checks that process on every pull request. Readiness checks the whole repository before you ship.

1. **Build**: your agents work as an engineering team, from the first idea to reviewed code. <https://apexyard.ai/build>
2. **Gate**: the check your reviewers see in each pull request. <https://apexyard.ai/gate>
3. **Readiness**: know what is safe to ship, area by area. <https://apexyard.ai/readiness>

## Free and Team

- **Free**: the hosted check on every pull request, in warning mode, on your own repository. No named approval.
- **Team**: the same check on every repository, named approval set up with you, a record for each merge, and one view of the organisation. See <https://apexyard.ai/pricing>.
- **The framework**: free and open source under the MIT licence. It needs no account and no dashboard.

## Install free

```sh
curl -fsSL https://apexyard.ai/install | sh
# or: brew install me2resh/tap/apexyard
# or: npx create-apexyard
cd your-project
apexyard init
/setup
```

66 hooks guard each edit, commit and push on the developer's machine. Every rule, hook and review agent is a plain file you can read, change or remove.

## Book a demo

Bring one of your repositories, and see what the Gate would have held. Book from <https://apexyard.ai/#book-a-demo>.

